cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Code, results and pre-registration for: Hard Constraints or Penalties? Temperature Extrapolation of MOF and COF Water Isotherms
message: If you use this software or its results, please cite it.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Abdulhamid
    family-names: Batayhi
    email: abdulhamid.batayhi@std.yildiz.edu.tr
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0007-0374-6755"
    affiliation: >-
      Yildiz Technical University, Faculty of Mechanical Engineering,
      Department of Mechatronics Engineering, Istanbul, Türkiye
version: v1.0.0
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.24120765
repository-code:"https://github.com/abdulhamidbatayhi123/ai-isotherm-thermo"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  A pre-registered factorial test of hard against penalty shape constraints (monotonicity in pressure, Henry
  limit) for the temperature extrapolation of measured water isotherms of 13 metal-organic and covalent organic
  frameworks, with the isosteric heat tested on synthetic truths with exact heats. Includes the frozen
  pre-registration and manifest, the confirmatory run records, a separately written second scorer, post-verdict
  diagnostics and a public correction ledger.
keywords:
  - metal-organic frameworks
  - covalent organic frameworks
  - water adsorption
  - isotherm
  - isosteric heat
  - physics-informed machine learning
  - pre-registration
